  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Massachusetts total $13B for FY2026 to date, with an award count of 72,992 and an average award size of $178K. Obligations fell 32.8% year over year. The state’s FY series shows a peak at $24.2B in FY21, followed by $17.9B in FY22, $18.3B in FY23, $17.8B in FY24, $19.3B in FY25, and $13B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer with $10B in obligations. Other top buying agencies are the Department of Veterans Affairs at $717M, the Department of Transportation at $703M, and the Department of Health and Human Services at $414M. Major vendors include RAYTHEON COMPANY at $2.9B, GENERAL ELECTRIC COMPANY at $1.2B, and RAYTHEON COMPANY again at $1B. Key industry concentrations are in aerospace and defense-related manufacturing and engineering services, with the top NAICS categories showing $2.9B in Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing and $1.6B in Engineering Services.",
